<title>SLOVENIA: Lek 96 net up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Lek 96 net up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian pharmaceutical producer Lek said on Friday 1996 net profit rose 14 percent to 2.88 billion tolars ($18.4 million), keeping pace with a 14 percent increase in sales to 38.2 billion tolars.</p>
<p>The company, which is among Slovenia's 10 largest firms, posted a pre-tax profit of 3.5 billion tolars and said it aimed to boost that figure by 20 percent in 1997. It forecast sales growth of another 14 percent.</p>
<p>Lek's A issue shares were trading almost six percent down in Ljubljana mid-morning at 22,800 tolars. Traders traced the delcine to the share going ex-dividend. -- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439 ($ = 156.6 Slovenia Tolars)</p>
</text>
